 ## Rules
 
 1. **A Folder has no path string.** `path` (a string) and `breadcrumb` (an array of Folders, root → self) are **derived getters** that walk `parent` up to the root. No model stores a path. A file's path is its folder's path plus its own name. `FileModel.path` is removed, and `UcpComponent.path` becomes derived. **No model stores a path under ANY name** — not `path`, not `filePath`, not smuggled into `description` or any other field (oopTester's inc-2 gate, 2026-09-29). **ONE named, counted, asserted-exercised allowance (oopPO ruling 2026-10-05, I4 RED-5; same form as rule 8's):** a `description` may cite a SPEC document as `spec/<name>.md`, and only when every such token RESOLVES to an existing file — a documentation reference, not a location of any unit. A source, component or `gen` path in a description is a defect: rewrite it to the CLASS name (location-free; a `move()` would make a path false). The allowance REDs a missing spec, a source path, a mixed value, and a spec path in any field other than `description`. **A root's path is its own name** — paths are relative to the tree's root, never absolute (ruled 2026-09-29, inc 2 flag 5).
-2. **Namespace is a Folder** — one Namespace per dotted segment. `static Namespace.declare(dotted, under)` — **`under` is REQUIRED**: there is no global root or registry (that would be a second namespace store through the back door; ruled 2026-09-29, inc 2 flag 2) — returns the leaf Namespace. **Names are unique per parent regardless of kind** — on disk a folder has one entry per name, so a same-named child is REUSED if it is a Namespace and is a NAMED ERROR if it is anything else; never a second sibling. A missing `under` is a named error too, never a raw TypeError and is **idempotent**: an existing child of the same name is reused, never duplicated (check-before-create). `namespace` (the dotted string) is derived from the breadcrumb: the segments BELOW `Components`, down to and including the Version, of every namespace-bearing kind — Namespace, UcpComponent (Package included), Version — skipping plain Folders. So `EAMD.ucp/Components/com/ceruleanCircle/Web4MDA/latest` derives **`com.ceruleanCircle.Web4MDA.latest`**, exactly Tron's `com.ceruleanCircle.Web4MDA.<version>`. Namespace is implemented by extending `DefaultFolder` — the concrete Folder — so it IS a Folder without re-implementing UcpComponent (inc 2 flag 1). This honours real ONCE 4.3.0, whose `Namespace.declare` derives the dotted name from the path with the version folder as a segment ([once.md](once.md)). **TWO namespaces, never merged (oopPO, 2026-10-05, from Tron's "obviously its relative!!!! no system dependencies"):** the MODEL namespace (`ClassModel.namespace`) is RELATIVE to the package and never empty — `Web4MDA`, `Web4MDA.MOF.M3`, `Web4MDA.Ior` — and is the ONE location fact; the FOLDER namespace derived here from the breadcrumb (`com.ceruleanCircle.Web4MDA.latest`) = the deployment prefix (where the package sits) + the model namespace + the Version. The model never stores the deployment prefix.
