 3. **Version is a Namespace inside a UcpComponent folder.** Its default name is `latest`, a synonym for git HEAD. The model admits siblings named after a semver tag (`1.0.0`, `2.4.5`), a branch or a commit hash. Only `latest` is generated now. **`latest` is created on demand and idempotently** (`Version.latest(component)`), never automatically: a Version is itself a component, so auto-creating `latest` would recurse (`latest/latest/…`; inc 2 flag 3). `Version.latest` over an existing non-Version child named `latest` is a named error — one `latest` per component, whatever tried to create it. A **tag is ONE segment**: `Version.named('1.0.0')` is a single folder `1.0.0`, never split into `1/0/0` (inc 2 flag 4 — a real bug caught).
 4. **A UcpComponent is a Folder** (it already `implements Folder`). Its content is `<Version>/{src,test}/<lang>/EAM/layerN/<file>`. A **Package** is a UcpComponent whose children are UcpComponents (~~it already binds `Container<UcpComponent>`~~ **via Tree's child parameter — `Container` retired 2026-09-30, [ucp.md](ucp.md) T1/T6**). A UcpComponent's children are **UcpUnits** (T6). Every nested component again has its own `latest`. **RULED by Tron 2026-09-30: a Package's sub-components live BESIDE its Version, not inside it** — `Web4MDA/<Component>/latest/` next to `Web4MDA/latest/`; they are direct children of the Package and are versioned independently of it. So a Package's `children` are its Versions AND its sub-components, never a filtered subset (ucp.md T6). **Nesting, 2026-10-05 (Tron, verbatim in [ucp.md](ucp.md) P):** this holds at EVERY depth — any component that contains components IS a Package, automatically: `Web4MDA/Ior/latest/` (Ior's own version) beside `Web4MDA/Ior/<Sub>/latest/`. A sub-component's folder is derived from its ~~`packagedIn` fact~~ **relative `namespace` (Tron, DRY — [thinglish.md](thinglish.md) rule 13)**, never from where its files happen to sit (generate relocates held sources to the derived folder — [component-model.md](component-model.md) rule 7).
