 7. **The root is found, not assumed.** Generation writes `<repository root>/EAMD.ucp` (bootstrap rule 8: always relative to the repository, no absolute path literal in any component's `latest/src/`). Looking for an *external* EAMD.ucp in the OS shared directories is a **structural exemption** owned by exactly one class — and it is **deferred**.
 8. **Import specifiers are derived from the layout.** Once classes sit in different folders, a generated file's import of another class is the RELATIVE path from the importing file's folder to the imported file — computed from the Folder tree (both breadcrumbs), never concatenated, never hand-written. (Hazard raised by oopExpert before increment 3; without it the generated JS stops executing.) **`ImportModel.from` is today a STORED relative path** (91 in the catalog, found by oopTester 2026-09-29): increment 3 replaces it by a reference to the imported CLASS, the specifier derived per this rule. **The value scan walks the catalog's REAL unit data, nested** — never only defaults — and every exception is a NAMED, COUNTED, ASSERTED-exercised allowance, never a silent skip: web URLs (`http`/`https` only — a `file:` URL is a filesystem path and is never allowed), npm manifest file fields (`main`, `types`, `startCommand`, `testCommand` — npm's contract), method bodies (code). Plain structural folders are identified by EXACT class, never by inheritance, so a future component built on `DefaultFolder` still counts in the namespace.
